{"id": "EUVD-2026-82021", "enisaUuid": "1f4e916a-adbd-3f2b-aa8d-3c302b47c188", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nregulator: core: use system_freezable_wq for init complete work\n\nschedule_delayed_work() uses system_wq, which is non-freezable, allowing\nregulator_init_complete_work to run concurrently with system suspend. This\nwork fires ~30s after boot to disable unused regulators via I2C. When it\nraces with PM suspend, the I2C adapter may already be suspended, triggering\na -ESHUTDOWN warning in __i2c_transfer():\n\n  WARNING: ... at __i2c_transfer+0x36c/0x3c8\n  Call trace:\n   __i2c_transfer\n   i2c_transfer\n   regmap_i2c_write\n   _regmap_update_bits\n   regulator_disable_regmap\n   _regulator_do_disable\n   regulator_late_cleanup\n   regulator_init_complete_work_function\n   process_one_work\n\nSwitch to system_freezable_wq so the work is frozen before any device\nis suspended, eliminating the race.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:02:16", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a2ae3ab348cce44120667277c2198f10cc348b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/350a0cba90e1bd40b1fe5b396923d2f3a61d1056", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2cebc00340a585adeffe321bc41f1937eb79a4dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9cf65270c1c1717c84dcfacd58a782c1186b0cbf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dc8570a5b830190bf0b57017c35aef97cd6ad7d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6d0a2c5e210f2fba099129e6183ef81316a6ae48", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0d23d658d79925076026fff62a49b8c94e0e8922", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b950aa7ec95e120b2bde745ca9a7ed3ce49d528", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29dc2e24f6adb36dcb884acf455644c397a67471", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/03eab318cedd6ae34ecd34533cd986edf5237164"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90360", "GHSA-8q97-2m9m-f966"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00eaaa5f-348e-3ed9-ade0-781b9b218d20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "09f89bd0-1ae8-3537-9327-876a7bd863a3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "55576cf1853798e86f620766e23b604c9224c19c <dc8570a5b830190bf0b57017c35aef97cd6ad7d9"}, {"id": "12298f05-037f-37b1-8e57-8b1cff68b03a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "55576cf1853798e86f620766e23b604c9224c19c <03eab318cedd6ae34ecd34533cd986edf5237164"}, {"id": "1cb601cd-82b4-3427-a3fb-3236dc0821c7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "25c1981e-72ed-302c-9cc6-2c51f94d24e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c4f65c2fb0f5c488d4ae606fba94bb98dcf383fd"}, {"id": "34b86ddc-f23d-319a-b295-8415397b7711", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "55576cf1853798e86f620766e23b604c9224c19c <9cf65270c1c1717c84dcfacd58a782c1186b0cbf"}, {"id": "3b79e05a-3954-312f-9418-81f981a459d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "55576cf1853798e86f620766e23b604c9224c19c <29dc2e24f6adb36dcb884acf455644c397a67471"}, {"id": "47716481-3b82-3977-9a15-82e3ae830c9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4"}, {"id": "47fbc3df-9875-37e6-b391-8c1ffc82fa84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.19.77 <4.20"}, {"id": "49bffad2-d2ef-3fbb-a5fa-bc577fab2fe2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8b8c8d69b1a31004517d4c71a490f47bdf3405a2 <8a2ae3ab348cce44120667277c2198f10cc348b1"}, {"id": "4afacaaf-09f7-3398-9121-3cff4f447ef5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.14.147 <4.14.160"}, {"id": "6a3cd1ff-525d-32c7-aaa0-700a61bd40f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}